nced]]\n* 2 red [[Cookbook:Chilli|chillies]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] 1 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]] thick\n* 2 green chillies, sliced 1 cm thick\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Scallion|scallions]] (white part only), sliced thin\n* 200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Bean Sprout|bean sprouts]], soaked in hot water\n* 25 g [[Cookbook:Parsley|fresh parsley]]\n* [[Cookbook:Duck|Duck meat]], sliced 1 cm thick\n* 600 g cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* 2 tbsp light [[Cookbook:Soy sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Habanero|habanero]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 1½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Heat the butter and sesame oil in a [[Cookbook:Non-stick|non-stick]] [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]] over medium-high heat. Add the garlic, chillies, and scallion. Fry, stirring, for 15 seconds until fragrant.\n# Add the duck meat, bean sprouts, and parsley. Stir until the duck meat changes color.\n# Add the rice, and then the soy sauce, habanero, black pepper, and salt. Stir until well-mixed.\n# Serve hot.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fried rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using duck]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bean sprout]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using soy sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using habanero chile]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Duck Fried Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 tbsp butter","sourceText":"3 tbsp butter","amountText":"3 tbsp butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp sesame oil","sourceText":"2 tbsp sesame oil","amountText":"2 tbsp sesame oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 cloves garlic, minced","sourceText":"3 cloves gar